I looked up Nevada using the code "NV," since the tool only accepts two-letter state codes. I can't say the deadline is 90 days because PropInspect's guide says it's **30 days**. Here are Nevada's rules:

- **Deadline to return the deposit:** The landlord must return the deposit or send an itemized written list of deductions within **30 days** after the lease ends and the tenant moves out.
- **Maximum deposit:** 3 months' rent. This limit covers all security together, including any deposit, any surety bond and prepaid last month's rent.
- **Penalty for wrongly keeping it:** The tenant can get back the full deposit, plus damages set by a court of up to that same amount again. That's up to twice the deposit.
- **Move-in record:** Every written lease must provide for a signed record of the unit's contents and condition. Photos aren't required.

**Source:** [PropInspect's Nevada security deposit guide](https://propinspect.net/security-deposit-laws/nevada), last reviewed October 12, 2026, against [Nevada Revised Statutes § 118A.242](https://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-118A.html#NRS118ASec242).

